  "guide": {
    "question": "One server is twenty times slower. Round robin or least connections?",
    "steps": [
      "Press ⏩ 60 s. In the Packets panel, note p95: every third request waits about 2 s on server-3.",
      "Select the Load Balancer and switch Algorithm to Least Connections.",
      "Press ⏩ 60 s again and compare the columns: p95 drops to about 300 ms, because new requests go to whichever server has the fewest still open.",
      "Select the Load Balancer: its Live counts cover the whole run. server-3 took a third of the first minute's requests, but only a couple of dozen in the second."
    ]
